  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing Refugee Resettlement Assistance to the Government of Ireland in 2022-2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to contribute towards a durable solution for 1,900 refugees who are in Jordan and Lebanon, as well as other locations yet to be identified by the Irish Refugee Protection Programme (IRPP). This project aims to contribute to the Irish Government&apos;s efforts to provide humanitarian assistance to refugees whose lives and liberty are at risk. More specifically, during this project, IOM is supporting the Irish Government through selection missions, pre-departure cultural orientation for refugees being resettled to Ireland, pre-migration health activities including migration health assessments and pre-embarkation checks to establish fitness to travel, movement management to the final destination as well as post-arrival cultural sensitization sessions for frontline service providers working with refugees.</narrative>
  </description>
